  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a member, I want the main screens (Favoris, Messages, Réglages, like Catégories) to open with their **large title**, which shrinks into the bar as I scroll, so that every top-level screen behaves the same and matches the current app.\n\n### Observed (operator, iPhone, 2026-11-16, current dev-swift)\n\n- **Catégories:** a large title « Catégories » at landing, collapsing to the inline title on scroll. ✓\n- **Favoris** (« Drapeaux », see #975), **Messages** and **Réglages:** the title is already small and inline at the top.\n- Screenshots kept locally by the operator.\n\n### Cause (read from the code)\n\n`.navigationBarTitleDisplayMode(.inline)` on `App/SwiftHFR/Messages/MessageListView.swift:34`, `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:53` and `App/SwiftHFR/Settings/SettingsView.swift:181`.\n\n### Legacy\n\nThe current app's Favoris and Messages open with a large title (the operator's screenshots of 2026-11-16 on #817 and #900). Cite the `navigationTitle` / display mode @ 87fe0d1c in the PR.\n\n### Wanted\n\n- Favoris, Messages and Réglages (and every other **root** list screen of a tab) use the `.large` title at landing, collapsing to inline on scroll, as Catégories does.\n- Pushed screens (a forum's topic list, the reader) keep their inline title.\n- Consistent with #865 (the title gets out of the way when scrolling): the large title is the landing state, then #865's behaviour applies. Check that the floating buttons (refresh, « ⋯ », compose) stay placed correctly in both states, and that the Messages segmented control (MP / MP multiples) sits under the large title.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The three screens land with a large title and collapse on scroll; a test on the display mode per root screen fails without the change.\n- [ ] Device check in the general review: iPhone portrait and landscape, iPad split.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
